[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
git-proxy caches FreeBSD pkg repositories (and many other package
registries) for the hosts on your network.

1. Set up the proxy

  cp %%ETCDIR%%/config.yaml.sample %%ETCDIR%%/config.yaml

  Set base_url to the URL your clients will use, e.g.
  "http://pkgproxy.example.org:8080", then:

  sysrc git_proxy_enable=YES
  service git_proxy start

  Cached data lives in %%GIT_PROXY_DBDIR%%. The dashboard at base_url
  shows hit rates and setup snippets.

2. Point pkg(8) at the proxy

  Each repository URL in /etc/pkg/FreeBSD.conf is made of an upstream
  base and a path:

    pkg+https://pkg.FreeBSD.org/${ABI}/quarterly
    \__________________________/\______________/
          upstream base              path

  To go through the proxy, keep the path and replace the upstream base
  with <base_url>/freebsd/trusted:

    http://pkgproxy.example.org:8080/freebsd/trusted/${ABI}/quarterly

  Drop the pkg+ prefix and set mirror_type to "none", since there are
  no SRV records for the proxy. Leave signature_type and fingerprints
  alone: catalogues are passed through unchanged and pkg still verifies
  them.

  On each client, create /usr/local/etc/pkg/repos/FreeBSD.conf:

    FreeBSD-ports: {
      url: "http://pkgproxy.example.org:8080/freebsd/trusted/${ABI}/quarterly",
      mirror_type: "none"
    }
    FreeBSD-ports-kmods: {
      url: "http://pkgproxy.example.org:8080/freebsd/trusted/${ABI}/kmods_quarterly_${VERSION_MINOR}",
      mirror_type: "none"
    }
    FreeBSD-base: {
      url: "http://pkgproxy.example.org:8080/freebsd/trusted/${ABI}/base_release_${VERSION_MINOR}",
      mirror_type: "none"
    }

  pkg fills in ${ABI} (e.g. FreeBSD:15:amd64, FreeBSD:16:aarch64) and
  ${VERSION_MINOR}, so the same file works on every host. Any set on
  pkg.FreeBSD.org works the same way: latest, release_N, kmods_latest,
  base_latest, base_weekly, and so on.

  Then run: pkg update -f

3. Other pkg repositories

  For a repository that is not on pkg.FreeBSD.org, split its URL into
  an upstream base and a path, give the base a name in
  %%ETCDIR%%/config.yaml, and restart git_proxy:

    url: "https://pkg.example.com/packages/150amd64-default"
          \______________________________/\_______________/
                  upstream base                 path

    upstream:
      freebsd:
        trusted: "https://pkg.freebsd.org"
        poudriere: "https://pkg.example.com/packages"

  Clients then use <base_url>/freebsd/<name>/<path>:

    url: "http://pkgproxy.example.org:8080/freebsd/poudriere/150amd64-default"

  Names are arbitrary labels. Keep the trusted entry: listing any
  repository replaces the built-in default. Only packages under
  Hashed/ are cached, so build such repositories with PKG_HASH=yes in
  poudriere.conf (pkg repo --hash).
EOM
}
]
